WEBVTT

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:04.560
Would you become research fellows
at my institute?

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.440
"Research fellows"?

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.730
It means special lab assistants.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:13.570
Satoshi and Go have become
research fellows at Sakuragi Institute.

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:16.070
They were intrigued by
Pokémon growing gigantic,

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:18.330
which led them to visit the Galar Region.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.710
Now, Pikachu! Electroweb!

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.300
At their first stop in Shoot City,

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.920
Satoshi had his backpack
stolen by Hibunny,

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.590
but he managed to get it back,

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:38.680
before boarding the train
to the Wild Area.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:41.640
The next day....

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:32.110
Looks delicious!

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:34.490
Thanks for the food!

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:49.380
You know, this bread
is really hard...

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:52.750
Well then, why don't you break it up
with your hands  before eating it?

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:56.880
Great idea!

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.940
I thought I saw something...

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.610
Must have imagined it.

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:18.780
Delicious!

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:20.240
What was that?

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.830
You try it, too!
It tastes better this way!

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:25.080
There's no way.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:34.550
This is great!

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:35.670
I know, right?

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:49.440
I am so sorry!

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:02.450
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:05.030
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:07.750
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:10.620
And skip the slow send-off

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.960
Be it through fire or through water

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.630
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:20.130
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:25.390
Each and every one of my memories

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:29.980
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:33.900
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:39.650
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:46.660
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:50.870
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.210
Let's have a fight!

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:54.920
1: Once the battle's done

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:56.750
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:03:56.750 --> 00:04:01.090
On 3, let's be friends!

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:07.760
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:13.100
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.610
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:19.730
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:21.490
I choose you!

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:30.500
The Mystery of Daimax!!
Kabigon Grows Giant?!

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:44.550
What?

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:14.960
All right, let's go find
a giant Pokémon!

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:17.920
Better get some pointers first.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:21.960
Excuse me.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:23.460
Can I help you?

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:26.840
I've heard there are Pokémon
that grow giant around here.

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:28.260
Do you know anything about it?

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:30.010
Grow giant?

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:32.260
Oh, you must mean Daimax.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:34.020
Daimax?

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:37.900
That's right. You can find it by
following the red lights.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:15.470
Wild Area, Galar Region

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.280
What are you looking at?

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:16.030
Are these the red lights
the station worker was talking about?

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:18.370
No, it couldn't be...

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:36.510
Is that...?

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:46.570
I see! Is this Daimax?

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:48.110
Awesome!

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:57.530
Kabigon! Sleeping Pokémon!
Normal type!

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:00.870
It eats 400 kilos of food every day!

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:04.630
It starts nodding off while eating—
and continues to eat even while it's asleep!

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:08.630
Its average height is 2.1 meters!

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:10.880
All right! Let's get recording!

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:12.130
Okay!

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:34.240
This Kabigon's height...

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:36.870
...is 3.2 meters!

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:39.240
Hey, Satoshi...

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:41.620
I...

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:44.620
...expected something grander.

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:47.630
Actually... so did I.

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:50.130
You think so, too?

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:51.550
Maybe Director Sakuragi...

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:56.970
...wanted to teach us that things aren't always as impressive
in real life as stories make them out to be.

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:01.770
It really isn't moving at all...

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:04.020
We should observe it
for a bit longer, I guess.

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:04.940
Yeah.

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:13.030
Go.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.820
Maybe Kabigon is
waiting for that to fall?

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:18.820
There's no way.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.290
It'd just grab that
if it wanted to eat it, yeah?

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:22.790
You think so?

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:45.180
You were right!

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:46.690
Ouch...

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:49.480
Who threw that rock?

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:55.860
Hibunny?!

00:09:57.110 --> 00:09:59.740
The one from yesterday?
But... it's not brown!

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:02.370
I see. It washed off the mud.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:05.290
You look better this way!

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.580
Were you following us?

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:11.130
I think it wants to come with you!

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:15.760
You really...?

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:23.890
I'm sorry.

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:30.520
I decided that
the first Pokémon I catch...

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:32.730
...will be Mew.

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:44.370
I made up my mind way back then.

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:51.920
If you really did follow me,
then I'm honored.

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:54.540
But... I'm sorry.

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:03.300
What's this?

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:09.890
Red lights!

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:11.060
Don't tell me...

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:28.160
Pocket Monsters!

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:37.500
. Normal .
Kabigon

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:46.140
Satoshi, what is this?!

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:47.220
How should I know?!

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:48.600
Run!

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:51.560
Hibunny! Follow me!

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:26.850
Hibunny!

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:33.850
Is this...

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:37.810
...what the station worker mentioned?
Daimax?

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:39.190
This is a <i>mountain!</i>

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:42.820
I mean, it's massive,
and there's even a <i>tree</i> up there!

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:46.450
This is bad, Satoshi!

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:49.990
What?! It's on the tracks!

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:52.200
A train will pass by here
in eight minutes!

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:53.120
What?!

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:58.790
Hey! Wake up, Kabigon!

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:00.380
Stand back, Go!

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:02.760
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:10.720
No use...

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:11.720
Satoshi!

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:17.690
That was close...

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:20.360
Is it moving in its sleep?

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:22.980
Whatever the case,
we have to move it, and fast!

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:26.240
Wake up, Kabigon!

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:29.070
Please, just wake up!

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:33.330
Wake… up!

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:35.040
Satoshi, look!

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:38.750
If we drop that berry...

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:45.090
It might move in order to eat it!

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:47.300
Got it! I'll give it a try!

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:48.260
Counting on you!

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:49.510
Pikachu!

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:51.510
Let's do this!

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:54.850
All right...

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:22.750
It's huge!

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:32.550
This is insane...

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:37.980
Where do we drop that?

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:43.690
Satoshi!

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:45.650
Drop the berry right here!

00:14:45.650 --> 00:14:46.480
Got it!

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:49.610
Pikachu, hit it with
an Iron Tail!

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:58.330
No good, huh?

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:00.330
Go! How much time left?!

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:01.920
Four more minutes!

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:03.540
Then it's all or nothing!

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:07.050
Pikachu!
Use a flurry of Iron Tails!

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:11.930
Come on!

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:15.640
Good, Pikachu!

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:19.140
One more!

00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:24.440
You did it!

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:25.570
I knew you could!

00:15:25.570 --> 00:15:27.780
Go, it's headed your way!

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:30.280
Good, keep it up!

00:15:31.150 --> 00:15:33.240
Go!

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:38.120
Not good!

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:43.250
Move!

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:46.250
Please, move!

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:58.010
Is it hopeless?

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:08.900
That's...!

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:15.160
All right! We're gonna
move it, for sure!

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:23.290
Pikachu!

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:29.460
Move...!

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:43.230
Hibunny, Double Kick!

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:45.940
Hit it with a Double Kick!

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:50.980
Do it!

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:01.790
All right!

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:31.730
Hibunny...

00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:36.240
Hey! You can't eat Hibunny!

00:17:56.010 --> 00:17:57.430
Thank goodness!

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:05.850
Hibunny, you did it!

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:11.190
Look! Your Double Kick
saved everyone!

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:21.200
Thanks!

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:49.980
Wait!

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:57.490
You were really cool!

00:18:58.240 --> 00:18:59.490
I've decided!

00:18:59.490 --> 00:19:03.240
The first Pokémon I catch will be you!

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:10.960
That okay with you?

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:19.010
Better catch you
with a curve ball, yeah?

00:19:20.760 --> 00:19:23.260
Monster Ball, go!

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:43.660
Did it work?

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:46.160
Don't worry! You got it!

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:47.450
Really?

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:52.670
Hibunny's data has been
added to the Index!

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:58.670
You did it, Go!

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:03.680
I caught my first Pokémon!

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:07.930
Hibunny, go!

00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:16.400
I look forward to working with you!

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:22.530
Looks like they'll make
a great team.

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:29.290
We're back!

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:32.410
Really? Kabigon's Daimax?

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:35.250
It was as big as a mountain!

00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:37.790
And it still managed to jump
at that size!

00:20:37.790 --> 00:20:40.800
Sounds like quite the experience!

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:47.390
What's wrong, Wanpachi?

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:52.560
Hibunny?

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:21.710
Go, is that...?

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:22.760
Let me introduce you!

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:25.090
This is my first-ever Pokémon;

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:27.640
Hibunny!

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:33.470
Satoshi and Go met a Daimax Pokémon
in the Galar Region...

00:21:33.470 --> 00:21:37.850
...and Go caught his
first-ever Pokémon; Hibunny!

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:42.360
Next time, more dreams and adventures
await in the world of Pocket Monsters!

